{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prop-s-polynomial-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:s-polynomial-decomposition","kind":"proposition","title":"$S$-polynomial decomposition of cancelling sums","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-admissible-system","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-groebner-basis"],"proofs":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prf-s-polynomial-decomposition"],"tags":["groebner-basis","s-polynomial"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.UnitalGroebner.s_polynomial_decomposition","text":"s-polynomial-decomposition.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial-decomposition.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:s-polynomial-decomposition\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a commutative ring with unity, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra which\nis free as an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> an\n<a href=\"#def:admissible-system\">admissible system</a>. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha \\in B</code> and\nsuppose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_1, \\ldots, f_n \\in A</code> satisfy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LM}(f_i) = \\alpha</code>\nand <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LC}(f_i) \\in R^\\times</code>. If</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  f := \\sum_i c_i f_i, \\qquad c_i \\in R^*,</code></pre>\n<p>satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LM}(f) &#x3C; \\alpha</code>, then we may write</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  f = \\sum_{i \\neq j} d_{i,j}\\, S_{i,j}</code></pre>\n<p>where the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_{i,j}</code> are the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code>-polynomials about <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_i</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f_j</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  S_{i,j} := \\frac{1}{a_i} f_i - \\frac{1}{a_j} f_j,\n  \\qquad a_i := \\mathrm{LC}(f_i),\\; a_j := \\mathrm{LC}(f_j) \\in R^\\times.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/s-polynomial-decomposition.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"2.4.4"}
